(321485, 24531, 4967, '<td valign="top">Personally I do not consider magazines to be in a horizontal shape... thats just me though.  I would have used slightly more DOF, although I like the nonexistant background, I think the picture would have looked a tad bit sharper with just a little more DOF...  The main part of the picture looks very centered... I think I might have cut out some of the right side of the photo, to make it a better picture.</td>', 'Personally I do not consider magazines to be in a horizontal shape... thats just me though.  I would have used slightly more DOF, although I like the nonexistant background, I think the picture would have looked a tad bit sharper with just a little more DOF...  The main part of the picture looks very centered... I think I might have cut out some of the right side of the photo, to make it a better picture.', '2003-06-11 02:58:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(321486, 24175, 9073, '<td valign="top">lovely, good line, good use of shallow dof, nice shutter speed to capture the movement in the wings. Perhaps a touch lighter would have been more effective. The light source is from top left but the main action is in the right hand side.</td>', 'lovely, good line, good use of shallow dof, nice shutter speed to capture the movement in the wings. Perhaps a touch lighter would have been more effective. The light source is from top left but the main action is in the right hand side.', '2003-06-11 02:59:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(321487, 23873, 4967, '<td valign="top">Personally I do not consider magazines to be in a horizontal shape... thats just me though.  This photo looks slightly tilted to me... but maybe it''s on a hillside.  Nice scene but I think you could have achieved a similar look by cutting out some of the left side to that back edge of the far hut.</td>', 'Personally I do not consider magazines to be in a horizontal shape... thats just me though.  This photo looks slightly tilted to me... but maybe it''s on a hillside.  Nice scene but I think you could have achieved a similar look by cutting out some of the left side to that back edge of the far hut.', '2003-06-11 03:00:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(321489, 24429, 7570, '<td valign="top">too much contrast on the bottom of the subject. contrast too high, details lost making the photo not very catchy. However, as a magazine cover, this is good.</td>', 'too much contrast on the bottom of the subject. contrast too high, details lost making the photo not very catchy. However, as a magazine cover, this is good.', '2003-06-11 03:02:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(321490, 24389, 4967, '<td valign="top">This is a busy scene... but that could say something about London.  I might have moved more to the left so that you didn''t have the guy on the left side in black in the photo... having just half of him is sort of distracting.. I might have used a different DOF so that the background was blurry.</td>', 'This is a busy scene... but that could say something about London.  I might have moved more to the left so that you didn''t have the guy on the left side in black in the photo... having just half of him is sort of distracting.. I might have used a different DOF so that the background was blurry.', '2003-06-11 03:02:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(321491, 24442, 9073, '<td valign="top">good capture of the action, nice line, vivid colours. maybe a bit underexposed on the skin</td>', 'good capture of the action, nice line, vivid colours. maybe a bit underexposed on the skin', '2003-06-11 03:03:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(321492, 24456, 9073, '<td valign="top">just a bit dark to see the detail in the lower half. the clouds work well, though</td>', 'just a bit dark to see the detail in the lower half. the clouds work well, though', '2003-06-11 03:04:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(321493, 24055, 4967, '<td valign="top">Is there actually this magazine?  Hehehe... thats funny.  The shadow on this is very annoying... I think it takes away from the look of the photo.  I would have played with my lighting more.  The melding off the floor with the wall is kind of bothersome in the photo... and it seems to come right out of the ducks head.  Also it makes the photo look tilted.  It might have been nice had you gotten dow to the carvings level or even below and shot.. this looks straight down, or from quite a bit higher.</td>', 'Is there actually this magazine?  Hehehe... thats funny.  The shadow on this is very annoying... I think it takes away from the look of the photo.  I would have played with my lighting more.  The melding off the floor with the wall is kind of bothersome in the photo... and it seems to come right out of the ducks head.  Also it makes the photo look tilted.  It might have been nice had you gotten dow to the carvings level or even below and shot.. this looks straight down, or from quite a bit higher.', '2003-06-11 03:05:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(321496, 24343, 9073, '<td valign="top">if you had used a slightly deeper dof to capture more of the body sharply, this would have been a magnificent shot. Even the leaf could afford to be sharper, I feel.</td>', 'if you had used a slightly deeper dof to capture more of the body sharply, this would have been a magnificent shot. Even the leaf could afford to be sharper, I feel.', '2003-06-11 03:05:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(321497, 24217, 9073, '<td valign="top">"Local Skateboarding" would have been a better title. There are 2 things that I really like in this shot - 1. The use of space below the jumping boy. There''s a dynamic movement here. 2. The line of heads drawing us through the frame.</td>', '"Local Skateboarding" would have been a better title. There are 2 things that I really like in this shot - 1. The use of space below the jumping boy. There''s a dynamic movement here. 2. The line of heads drawing us through the frame.', '2003-06-11 03:07:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(321498, 24390, 9073, '<td valign="top">The blue cast is too strong and makes the ice look unnatural. Otherwise, a very capturing image.</td>', 'The blue cast is too strong and makes the ice look unnatural. Otherwise, a very capturing image.', '2003-06-11 03:08:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(321499, 24437, 4967, '<td valign="top">Sexy... you definitely had a good model for this one.  In terms of a photo that SI might use for their cover their are some problems here.  The lighting here is not optimal... that is one thing that SI is very adament about for their swimsuit edition, a lot of the girl is in shadow, especially her face, which is bothersome.  The border probably shouldn''t have been added as I don''t believe Si uses a border for their magazine, and if they do it''s definitely not the thick, also the photo comes so close to the girls head that it almost seems to cut off some of her hair.  I am also not sure where the title would go on this magazine cover, or any of the info on what is in the magazine.  Good try though... could definitely start to be an inside photo for SI, but prolly not a cover.</td>', 'Sexy... you definitely had a good model for this one.  In terms of a photo that SI might use for their cover their are some problems here.  The lighting here is not optimal... that is one thing that SI is very adament about for their swimsuit edition, a lot of the girl is in shadow, especially her face, which is bothersome.  The border probably shouldn''t have been added as I don''t believe Si uses a border for their magazine, and if they do it''s definitely not the thick, also the photo comes so close to the girls head that it almost seems to cut off some of her hair.  I am also not sure where the title would go on this magazine cover, or any of the info on what is in the magazine.  Good try though... could definitely start to be an inside photo for SI, but prolly not a cover.', '2003-06-11 03:09:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(321500, 24237, 4967, '<td valign="top">Corn/fox snake?  What a beautiful animal.  Is that how his eyes normally are?  Since I''m guessing this is a pet snake I would have like to have seen him in a more natural environlment... or at least stretched out some.  You also lose a lot of detail in the whiteness or lightness of the shavings at the bottom of the photo, which detract from the photo... The snake is also too centered in this photo, I think, cropping in from all sides might have helped, although maybe this leaves sufficient room for words?  I think I would have tried to make the snake a more substantial part of the overall photo.</td>', 'Corn/fox snake?  What a beautiful animal.  Is that how his eyes normally are?  Since I''m guessing this is a pet snake I would have like to have seen him in a more natural environlment... or at least stretched out some.  You also lose a lot of detail in the whiteness or lightness of the shavings at the bottom of the photo, which detract from the photo... The snake is also too centered in this photo, I think, cropping in from all sides might have helped, although maybe this leaves sufficient room for words?  I think I would have tried to make the snake a more substantial part of the overall photo.', '2003-06-11 03:13:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(321501, 24500, 9073, '<td valign="top">Here''s looking at you, kid. <br/>The stray petal at the bottom and the stem on the right detract from the overall effect.</td>', 'Here''s looking at you, kid. The stray petal at the bottom and the stem on the right detract from the overall effect.', '2003-06-11 03:13:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(321503, 24447, 9136, '<td valign="top">I don''t really care for the border on this one, but the colors are great and I love the grainy feel. 9.</td>', 'I don''t really care for the border on this one, but the colors are great and I love the grainy feel. 9.', '2003-06-11 03:15:08.000000', NULL, 1),
