(322599, 24447, 5391, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous!  The tones are beautiful.  9</td>', 'Gorgeous!  The tones are beautiful.  9', '2003-06-11 17:42:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(322601, 24003, 8140, '<td valign="top">it is a little bit blurry. = 4</td>', 'it is a little bit blurry. = 4', '2003-06-11 17:43:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(322605, 24048, 5391, '<td valign="top">The blown out hotspots are a problem for me in this shot.  Espcially with fashion photography, to be up there with the best of them doing magazine covers, lighting is so important.  However, the model, her dress and the pose are all extremely good.  I''d try it again with more diffuse light.</td>', 'The blown out hotspots are a problem for me in this shot.  Espcially with fashion photography, to be up there with the best of them doing magazine covers, lighting is so important.  However, the model, her dress and the pose are all extremely good.  I''d try it again with more diffuse light.', '2003-06-11 17:44:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(322607, 24427, 8140, '<td valign="top">I like shadow, it is very cool shot! = 8</td>', 'I like shadow, it is very cool shot! = 8', '2003-06-11 17:45:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(322608, 24456, 5391, '<td valign="top">Holy cow.  What an incredible place.  You could really have a lot of fun with this setting for all kinds of photographic potentials...  As far as the challenge goes, I think you''ve done very well.  Interesting subject matter, great clouds, great composition.  Maybe a bit on the yellow side, but overall I like this very much!</td>', 'Holy cow.  What an incredible place.  You could really have a lot of fun with this setting for all kinds of photographic potentials...  As far as the challenge goes, I think you''ve done very well.  Interesting subject matter, great clouds, great composition.  Maybe a bit on the yellow side, but overall I like this very much!', '2003-06-11 17:46:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(322615, 24402, 8530, '<td valign="top">It''s a pretty photo with nice lighting -- I like the hazy lighting come through the trees and the small bit of bright up near the top. I don''t know your magazine and haven''t looked it up, so I''m judging by title alone. It is a country-looking scene (at least it is a non-urban looking one) so it''s obviously somewhat topical, though I''m wondering if a ''Country Living'' would be more inclined to show a scene that seems more inhabited than this; it helps you have a solid path running through the left bottom corner, so it doesn''t feel entirely remote.</td>', 'It''s a pretty photo with nice lighting -- I like the hazy lighting come through the trees and the small bit of bright up near the top. I don''t know your magazine and haven''t looked it up, so I''m judging by title alone. It is a country-looking scene (at least it is a non-urban looking one) so it''s obviously somewhat topical, though I''m wondering if a ''Country Living'' would be more inclined to show a scene that seems more inhabited than this; it helps you have a solid path running through the left bottom corner, so it doesn''t feel entirely remote.', '2003-06-11 17:49:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(322621, 24430, 8291, '<td valign="top">This picture really makes me think of Vogue! Good job! You get a 10 from me ;-)</td>', 'This picture really makes me think of Vogue! Good job! You get a 10 from me ;-)', '2003-06-11 17:55:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(322622, 24190, 8530, '<td valign="top">Hadn''t heard of your magazine before this but it doesn''t surprise me in the least an industry-specific magazine like this exists. The photo fits the topic. I think its possible the reflection in the building shows up a little TOO well, maybe because of how highly-lit it is, in terms of attractiveness of photo, though if that were the point of the article I suppose that would make sense. I just am not sure where a compositor would fit text easily. As an industry-style magazine photo it''s fine even if I wouldn''t exactly hang it on my wall.</td>', 'Hadn''t heard of your magazine before this but it doesn''t surprise me in the least an industry-specific magazine like this exists. The photo fits the topic. I think its possible the reflection in the building shows up a little TOO well, maybe because of how highly-lit it is, in terms of attractiveness of photo, though if that were the point of the article I suppose that would make sense. I just am not sure where a compositor would fit text easily. As an industry-style magazine photo it''s fine even if I wouldn''t exactly hang it on my wall.', '2003-06-11 17:56:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(322623, 24337, 3669, '<td valign="top">The clouds are absolutely breathtaking and the mountains in the background are nice.  This is a lovely picture and it''s done well, but I don''t actually see this as a magazine cover.  Why?  Because I don''t know how it could be edited to fit the dimensions of the cover.  If you crop out the viewer''s right, you cut out the clouds and if you crop left, you have the clouds, but cut out the boat and people in the water.  I would actually see this picture on the inside of the magazine featuring this place in an article.  8  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'The clouds are absolutely breathtaking and the mountains in the background are nice.  This is a lovely picture and it''s done well, but I don''t actually see this as a magazine cover.  Why?  Because I don''t know how it could be edited to fit the dimensions of the cover.  If you crop out the viewer''s right, you cut out the clouds and if you crop left, you have the clouds, but cut out the boat and people in the water.  I would actually see this picture on the inside of the magazine featuring this place in an article.  8  Good luck in the challenge.', '2003-06-11 17:56:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(322626, 24429, 8530, '<td valign="top">Topically the photograph is fine, I can easily see this on New Scientist with the right article. I think you would have been better off with not quite so bright of lighting glow. The fade on the light would also have been softer which would help the compositor. The sharp focus on the top edge of the focus is good but it loses some at the bottom edge of the rim because of the lighting as well.</td>', 'Topically the photograph is fine, I can easily see this on New Scientist with the right article. I think you would have been better off with not quite so bright of lighting glow. The fade on the light would also have been softer which would help the compositor. The sharp focus on the top edge of the focus is good but it loses some at the bottom edge of the rim because of the lighting as well.', '2003-06-11 17:59:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(322630, 24460, 4967, '<td valign="top">Wow very pretty, if this is your house, this is really cool, congrats!  I think this would do nicely as a cover of a magazine... I''m not sure about the border, I''m not big on borders, and I don''t think most magazine covers have borders, but it''s not too big of a deal.  This is a plain simple nice looking photo that fits the challenge.  Good job.</td>', 'Wow very pretty, if this is your house, this is really cool, congrats!  I think this would do nicely as a cover of a magazine... I''m not sure about the border, I''m not big on borders, and I don''t think most magazine covers have borders, but it''s not too big of a deal.  This is a plain simple nice looking photo that fits the challenge.  Good job.', '2003-06-11 18:03:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(322633, 24490, 8530, '<td valign="top">This is a wonderful photo in general; I love the lighting, it''s very crisp, it''s a good angle to do this from.<br/> <br/>Topically it fits your magazine choice well.<br/> <br/>My only complaint would be from a compositor standpoint. There''s room for the logo and other top matter, but it would be difficult on a shot with this much colour contrast to fit in coverlines. I see a couple spaces where one could do it (the water, above the bridge) but it''d be tight to work with it. It''s possible some judicious desaturation or other adjustment would fix this, though.</td>', 'This is a wonderful photo in general; I love the lighting, it''s very crisp, it''s a good angle to do this from. Topically it fits your magazine choice well. My only complaint would be from a compositor standpoint. There''s room for the logo and other top matter, but it would be difficult on a shot with this much colour contrast to fit in coverlines. I see a couple spaces where one could do it (the water, above the bridge) but it''d be tight to work with it. It''s possible some judicious desaturation or other adjustment would fix this, though.', '2003-06-11 18:04:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(322634, 24210, 8242, '<td valign="top">nice photo, should have cropped whatever that is in the bottom right corner.</td>', 'nice photo, should have cropped whatever that is in the bottom right corner.', '2003-06-11 18:04:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(322635, 24392, 4967, '<td valign="top">Hmmmm... I''m not sure my decision on this photo... I guess it could fit the said magazine, but I''m just not sure it''s particularly attractive or something that really catches the eye.  Not sure, but I think there is much too much blank space.</td>', 'Hmmmm... I''m not sure my decision on this photo... I guess it could fit the said magazine, but I''m just not sure it''s particularly attractive or something that really catches the eye.  Not sure, but I think there is much too much blank space.', '2003-06-11 18:04:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(322637, 24209, 8530, '<td valign="top">Never heard of your magazine but wouldn''t surprise me if it existed. With that in mind and the subtitle...<br/> <br/>The shot is actually not bad in terms of lighting or focus but I''d think a truck magazine would want a less tight shot on the logo and show a bit more of the truck itself. The logo also takes up enough of the shot width-wise that I''m wondering how cropping, if necessary, would work. There''s certainly plenty of homogenous room to fit text and logos in, however, which helps.</td>', 'Never heard of your magazine but wouldn''t surprise me if it existed. With that in mind and the subtitle... The shot is actually not bad in terms of lighting or focus but I''d think a truck magazine would want a less tight shot on the logo and show a bit more of the truck itself. The logo also takes up enough of the shot width-wise that I''m wondering how cropping, if necessary, would work. There''s certainly plenty of homogenous room to fit text and logos in, however, which helps.', '2003-06-11 18:05:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(322639, 24197, 4967, '<td valign="top">Hmmm... not sure I really care for this or think it fits... not familiar with the magazine, but I don''t think it would work.  I just don''t think this is a very effective photo.</td>', 'Hmmm... not sure I really care for this or think it fits... not familiar with the magazine, but I don''t think it would work.  I just don''t think this is a very effective photo.', '2003-06-11 18:06:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(322641, 24390, 8758, '<td valign="top">I really like the composition.... the colour is fabulous....the overly white highlights on the ice in the sea and the black dashes on the top left of the iceberg disrupt the visual flow. I wanted it to be my perfect 10 :-(</td>', 'I really like the composition.... the colour is fabulous....the overly white highlights on the ice in the sea and the black dashes on the top left of the iceberg disrupt the visual flow. I wanted it to be my perfect 10 :-(', '2003-06-11 18:07:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(322642, 24338, 4967, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous use of this type of photo.  Excellent example.  I''m not sure it really fits the magazine, but it''s very well done.  I think it could be the cover of a magazine just not necessarily the one you picked.  beautifully done though!</td>', 'Gorgeous use of this type of photo.  Excellent example.  I''m not sure it really fits the magazine, but it''s very well done.  I think it could be the cover of a magazine just not necessarily the one you picked.  beautifully done though!', '2003-06-11 18:07:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(322644, 24339, 8530, '<td valign="top">Haven''t heard of your magazine but I know there are a jillion craft-related magazines out there so no surprise.<br/> <br/>This is an ideal photo. It obviously fits a specific article type, it''s a pretty, well-lit photo, and there''s enough hats showing that any crop required would still work out. About the only place it might suffer slightly is in text composition and if this isn''t a full-bleed magazine photo that works out fine. If it is, it might be a little tough to work around the colourful ribbons, though it would be possible, especially if the crop focussed on the left, so it''s only a minor flaw at worst.</td>', 'Haven''t heard of your magazine but I know there are a jillion craft-related magazines out there so no surprise. This is an ideal photo. It obviously fits a specific article type, it''s a pretty, well-lit photo, and there''s enough hats showing that any crop required would still work out. About the only place it might suffer slightly is in text composition and if this isn''t a full-bleed magazine photo that works out fine. If it is, it might be a little tough to work around the colourful ribbons, though it would be possible, especially if the crop focussed on the left, so it''s only a minor flaw at worst.', '2003-06-11 18:07:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(322647, 24517, 4967, '<td valign="top">Interesting idea... I think it works, though it bothers me how the top left corner starts to get blurry.  Otherwise I think it is a simple idea that could possibly be used for a magazine cover.</td>', 'Interesting idea... I think it works, though it bothers me how the top left corner starts to get blurry.  Otherwise I think it is a simple idea that could possibly be used for a magazine cover.', '2003-06-11 18:09:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(322648, 24208, 8530, '<td valign="top">I can easily see something like this on a natural-history exhibit focus in the Smithsonian.<br/> <br/>It might be slightly too tight a focus as a further crop would make the object harder to identify, but it isn''t out of the question. There''s enough colour neutrality to easily allow for the placement of coverlines without ruining the intensity of the photo.</td>', 'I can easily see something like this on a natural-history exhibit focus in the Smithsonian. It might be slightly too tight a focus as a further crop would make the object harder to identify, but it isn''t out of the question. There''s enough colour neutrality to easily allow for the placement of coverlines without ruining the intensity of the photo.', '2003-06-11 18:10:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(322651, 24500, 8530, '<td valign="top">Slightly more vague than I might have invisioned on a Martha Stewart cover but not out of the question by any means. (By ''vague'' I mean the cover art tends to focus on, say, a whole flowerbed or a project involving flowers more than it would a single bloom but that''s on limited experience, I admit.)<br/> <br/>I like the shot a lot. It''s got great colour contrast, and the focal blur in the back makes the ideal backdrop for coverlines. The only place it suffers at all is fitting the logo at the top without obscuring the flower, which is minor; they might choose to continue the green colour up into an added background to compensate.</td>', 'Slightly more vague than I might have invisioned on a Martha Stewart cover but not out of the question by any means. (By ''vague'' I mean the cover art tends to focus on, say, a whole flowerbed or a project involving flowers more than it would a single bloom but that''s on limited experience, I admit.) I like the shot a lot. It''s got great colour contrast, and the focal blur in the back makes the ideal backdrop for coverlines. The only place it suffers at all is fitting the logo at the top without obscuring the flower, which is minor; they might choose to continue the green colour up into an added background to compensate.', '2003-06-11 18:13:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(322653, 24454, 4967, '<td valign="top">Very nice... I''m not sure I would have put this as National Geographic... but maybe.  I think it would have been nice to have the bee just slightly more in focus.  Very well done though... could definitely be a magazine cover, if not NG then maybe something else.  very pretty, hope you didn''t get stung!</td>', 'Very nice... I''m not sure I would have put this as National Geographic... but maybe.  I think it would have been nice to have the bee just slightly more in focus.  Very well done though... could definitely be a magazine cover, if not NG then maybe something else.  very pretty, hope you didn''t get stung!', '2003-06-11 18:13:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(322655, 24438, 4967, '<td valign="top">Nice, though isn''t Highlights usually a drawn cover?  I don''t think it usually has photos on it does it?  I like this photo, could definitely see it on the front of a cover.  i don''t like the border though, I don''t think it helps, and I''m not sure many magazines have a border.  Nice night photo though... I think it''s definitely well done.</td>', 'Nice, though isn''t Highlights usually a drawn cover?  I don''t think it usually has photos on it does it?  I like this photo, could definitely see it on the front of a cover.  i don''t like the border though, I don''t think it helps, and I''m not sure many magazines have a border.  Nice night photo though... I think it''s definitely well done.', '2003-06-11 18:14:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(322657, 24362, 8530, '<td valign="top">Haven''t heard of your magazine but I know there are golfer mags out there so I''m cool with that.<br/> <br/>It''s a pretty landscape shot that is a little less obviously a golf course than I would have chosen, but the flag in the background does give it context (and of course it would have a different context once cover copy was added). The shot is crisp and clean, it shows off what would probably be a challenging part of a course, from what little I know of golf. The focal blur on the background gives plenty of space for cover copy, as does the reasonable homogenity of the grass. A crop would not ruin it in the case of a full-bleed image. Overall a good job, however little I like golf. :)</td>', 'Haven''t heard of your magazine but I know there are golfer mags out there so I''m cool with that. It''s a pretty landscape shot that is a little less obviously a golf course than I would have chosen, but the flag in the background does give it context (and of course it would have a different context once cover copy was added). The shot is crisp and clean, it shows off what would probably be a challenging part of a course, from what little I know of golf. The focal blur on the background gives plenty of space for cover copy, as does the reasonable homogenity of the grass. A crop would not ruin it in the case of a full-bleed image. Overall a good job, however little I like golf. :)', '2003-06-11 18:15:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(322658, 24236, 326, '<td valign="top">I would have loved to see a person using this tool in the photo.</td>', 'I would have loved to see a person using this tool in the photo.', '2003-06-11 18:16:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(322659, 24470, 4967, '<td valign="top">Personally I do not consider magazines to be in a horizontal shape... thats just me though.  Beautiful waterfall though!  Not sure where you would put the type.  As a photo its very nice, but as a magazine cover, it just doesn''t fit IMHO.  Sorry.</td>', 'Personally I do not consider magazines to be in a horizontal shape... thats just me though.  Beautiful waterfall though!  Not sure where you would put the type.  As a photo its very nice, but as a magazine cover, it just doesn''t fit IMHO.  Sorry.', '2003-06-11 18:16:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(322661, 23990, 326, '<td valign="top">Beautiful Portrait!</td>', 'Beautiful Portrait!', '2003-06-11 18:19:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(322662, 24213, 4967, '<td valign="top">Very nice... really works for that magazine, with plenty of space for type.  I like it... it''s not a wow photo, but it works.  Not much to say here except that I think it fits... but it''s a little far off for a magazine... I think getting below the house would have been nice, and shooting up with the mountains towering over it could have been really cool.  That''s just my opinion though.</td>', 'Very nice... really works for that magazine, with plenty of space for type.  I like it... it''s not a wow photo, but it works.  Not much to say here except that I think it fits... but it''s a little far off for a magazine... I think getting below the house would have been nice, and shooting up with the mountains towering over it could have been really cool.  That''s just my opinion though.', '2003-06-11 18:19:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(322663, 24101, 9327, '<td valign="top">a quiet setting with very nice lighting, and a sportscar.. looks surreal..<br/></td>', 'a quiet setting with very nice lighting, and a sportscar.. looks surreal..', '2003-06-11 18:19:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(322665, 24343, 4967, '<td valign="top">Nothing really looks completely in focus here.  It''s kind of bothersome and out of focus.  Interesting, and I like the fact you left room at the top for type, but I''m just not sure the photo is fabulous.  Very nice job getting so close though!</td>', 'Nothing really looks completely in focus here.  It''s kind of bothersome and out of focus.  Interesting, and I like the fact you left room at the top for type, but I''m just not sure the photo is fabulous.  Very nice job getting so close though!', '2003-06-11 18:20:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(322666, 24215, 9327, '<td valign="top">funny, but the composition/or woman should have been raised 1 mtr so that everything looked centered</td>', 'funny, but the composition/or woman should have been raised 1 mtr so that everything looked centered', '2003-06-11 18:21:00.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(322669, 23969, 4967, '<td valign="top">Wow now thats a lot of bikes!  Interesting, not sure if it''s more a snapshot then really a professional photo for a magazine though.  I like the fact you have space at the top for type, though I think getting down and filling the frame with bikes and leaving it so you could have the type over that might have been more effectual for this shot.  That''s just my opinion though.</td>', 'Wow now thats a lot of bikes!  Interesting, not sure if it''s more a snapshot then really a professional photo for a magazine though.  I like the fact you have space at the top for type, though I think getting down and filling the frame with bikes and leaving it so you could have the type over that might have been more effectual for this shot.  That''s just my opinion though.', '2003-06-11 18:21:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(322671, 23950, 4967, '<td valign="top">I used to love this magazine!  This is a great photo for it... The DoF could have been slightly different so you had the whole bird in focus, but thats not imperitive.  Was this taken at a zoo?  I like how you left space at the top for type.  This isn''t a WOW photo, but it''s still good, one of the better shots for the challenge.</td>', 'I used to love this magazine!  This is a great photo for it... The DoF could have been slightly different so you had the whole bird in focus, but thats not imperitive.  Was this taken at a zoo?  I like how you left space at the top for type.  This isn''t a WOW photo, but it''s still good, one of the better shots for the challenge.', '2003-06-11 18:22:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(322675, 24140, 3697, '<td valign="top">What a great shot! perfect focus and lighting, and excellent DOF. The black background really helps to highlight the cigar smoke. The onli knitpick I have (and it''s a very small one) would have been to either move the cigar to the left or crop less off the right, just so the smoke wasn''t cut off. But like I said, the picture absolutely excellent as is and definately one of the week''s best.</td>', 'What a great shot! perfect focus and lighting, and excellent DOF. The black background really helps to highlight the cigar smoke. The onli knitpick I have (and it''s a very small one) would have been to either move the cigar to the left or crop less off the right, just so the smoke wasn''t cut off. But like I said, the picture absolutely excellent as is and definately one of the week''s best.', '2003-06-11 18:24:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(322676, 24390, 3697, '<td valign="top">Very nice, excellent composition. The different shades of blue work together very well here.</td>', 'Very nice, excellent composition. The different shades of blue work together very well here.', '2003-06-11 18:25:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(322689, 24319, 3697, '<td valign="top">I like it. :) Having the photographer as a sillhouette (sp?) was a great idea. To me, it shows the photographer but more than that, it helps to highlight what the photographer is photographing. Very cool.</td>', 'I like it. :) Having the photographer as a sillhouette (sp?) was a great idea. To me, it shows the photographer but more than that, it helps to highlight what the photographer is photographing. Very cool.', '2003-06-11 18:33:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(322692, 23968, 9098, '<td valign="top">I really like the "expression" you caputured on the horse''s face!  Good timing!</td>', 'I really like the "expression" you caputured on the horse''s face!  Good timing!', '2003-06-11 18:33:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(322694, 24339, 9098, '<td valign="top">Very colorful.  Nice cropping.</td>', 'Very colorful.  Nice cropping.', '2003-06-11 18:34:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(322696, 24509, 3697, '<td valign="top">Great lighting, and having the water drops on the pear is a definate plus. Oh, and the black background... two thumbs up. :)</td>', 'Great lighting, and having the water drops on the pear is a definate plus. Oh, and the black background... two thumbs up. :)', '2003-06-11 18:34:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(322701, 24354, 4122, '<td valign="top">great photo and idea ... except i don''t really care for the border.</td>', 'great photo and idea ... except i don''t really care for the border.', '2003-06-11 18:37:31.000000', NULL, 1),
