(323180, 24507, 4967, '<td valign="top">This is cool... what piece of equipment is this?  I love mac''s... I think it''s the only way to go.  I could definitely see this on the cover Mac Addict.  I think there is perhaps too much light in the bottom left, but the rest is really good... Nicely done.  Hope you don''t get ripped on for using a Mac.</td>', 'This is cool... what piece of equipment is this?  I love mac''s... I think it''s the only way to go.  I could definitely see this on the cover Mac Addict.  I think there is perhaps too much light in the bottom left, but the rest is really good... Nicely done.  Hope you don''t get ripped on for using a Mac.', '2003-06-12 05:01:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(323181, 24424, 4967, '<td valign="top">Personally I do not consider magazines to be in a horizontal shape... thats just me though.  Is this an actual magazine?  I couldn''t find it online... what kind of things are in it?  I guess even with that name it doesn''t have a picture of a person smiling with a strawberry every month/week/quarter does it?  That strawberry kind of doesn''t look too good, it looks pretty old and not so pretty, I wouldn''t expect to see it on the cover of a magazine.  I like your DOF though.</td>', 'Personally I do not consider magazines to be in a horizontal shape... thats just me though.  Is this an actual magazine?  I couldn''t find it online... what kind of things are in it?  I guess even with that name it doesn''t have a picture of a person smiling with a strawberry every month/week/quarter does it?  That strawberry kind of doesn''t look too good, it looks pretty old and not so pretty, I wouldn''t expect to see it on the cover of a magazine.  I like your DOF though.', '2003-06-12 05:05:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(323182, 24447, 6359, '<td valign="top">A little grainy.</td>', 'A little grainy.', '2003-06-12 05:05:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(323183, 24501, 4967, '<td valign="top">Personally I do not consider magazines to be in a horizontal shape... thats just me though.  Is the matte board grey, or should you have increased the contrast some?  I guess I could see this on the said magazine... I think it depends on how high-tech the magazine gets.  Technically it''s a very good photo... I guess I would have liked to have seen it as a vertical instead of a horizontal, I think it would have improved it as a magazine cover, and probably improved your score as well.</td>', 'Personally I do not consider magazines to be in a horizontal shape... thats just me though.  Is the matte board grey, or should you have increased the contrast some?  I guess I could see this on the said magazine... I think it depends on how high-tech the magazine gets.  Technically it''s a very good photo... I guess I would have liked to have seen it as a vertical instead of a horizontal, I think it would have improved it as a magazine cover, and probably improved your score as well.', '2003-06-12 05:08:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(323184, 24527, 4967, '<td valign="top">Dead center of the page from right to left, not extremely interesting.  Doesn''t fill the frame at all, or even give us a good clear view of the moon.  Nothing much to look at here, but at least you made it vertical.</td>', 'Dead center of the page from right to left, not extremely interesting.  Doesn''t fill the frame at all, or even give us a good clear view of the moon.  Nothing much to look at here, but at least you made it vertical.', '2003-06-12 05:09:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(323185, 24115, 4967, '<td valign="top">Personally I do not consider magazines to be in a horizontal shape... thats just me though.  I like the red background you put this on... it kind of makes me think of blood but it seems fitting for a gun.  Man, I would not want to be hit with one of those bullets?  Are those the ones they call "hollowtips"?  Whatever they are I''m sure their lethal.  I''m sure this could be the front cover of a magazine.</td>', 'Personally I do not consider magazines to be in a horizontal shape... thats just me though.  I like the red background you put this on... it kind of makes me think of blood but it seems fitting for a gun.  Man, I would not want to be hit with one of those bullets?  Are those the ones they call "hollowtips"?  Whatever they are I''m sure their lethal.  I''m sure this could be the front cover of a magazine.', '2003-06-12 05:12:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(323186, 24300, 4967, '<td valign="top">Personally I do not consider magazines to be in a horizontal shape... thats just me though.  Is this a particularly nice plant?  It looks fairly crowded to me.  The lighting in this photo is somewhat bothersome, especially the glare in the upper left hand corner.  I think I would have liked to have seen less plant, more substance to the photo.</td>', 'Personally I do not consider magazines to be in a horizontal shape... thats just me though.  Is this a particularly nice plant?  It looks fairly crowded to me.  The lighting in this photo is somewhat bothersome, especially the glare in the upper left hand corner.  I think I would have liked to have seen less plant, more substance to the photo.', '2003-06-12 05:14:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(323187, 23968, 6359, '<td valign="top">The focus is great. I don''t really care for the open mouth look.</td>', 'The focus is great. I don''t really care for the open mouth look.', '2003-06-12 05:17:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(323188, 24258, 4967, '<td valign="top">You''ve got a tough situation here... a white dog on a green setting.  You lose some of the detail in the dog... to overcome this, I think you should try zooming in on the dog and taking a meter reading off of him (correct exposure)  then zooming out and manually setting the camera to the dogs meter reading, although the overall photo maybe a tad bit darker, I think it will help to get more detail on the dog and not just a white blob with some black.  The composition of your picture is pretty good... It looks like a nice peaceful setting something that could probably be on the front of the said magazine.  Not terribly exciting but a good wholesome job.</td>', 'You''ve got a tough situation here... a white dog on a green setting.  You lose some of the detail in the dog... to overcome this, I think you should try zooming in on the dog and taking a meter reading off of him (correct exposure)  then zooming out and manually setting the camera to the dogs meter reading, although the overall photo maybe a tad bit darker, I think it will help to get more detail on the dog and not just a white blob with some black.  The composition of your picture is pretty good... It looks like a nice peaceful setting something that could probably be on the front of the said magazine.  Not terribly exciting but a good wholesome job.', '2003-06-12 05:19:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(323205, 24533, 8643, '<td valign="top">Take a portrait crop of this - just the face and hand and you would have a winner!  The aspect ratio is wrong for a mgazine and the rest of the body is a distraction.</td>', 'Take a portrait crop of this - just the face and hand and you would have a winner!  The aspect ratio is wrong for a mgazine and the rest of the body is a distraction.', '2003-06-12 06:28:07.000000', NULL, 1),
