(328326, 24218, 4564, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everybody who left comments.  I appreciate the fact that most of you were very respectful in your comments even though the photo was riské for DPC.<br/> <br/>I knew when submiting this photo that it was risky.  But I honestly question its ranking position... I think it deserved more, especially in the context of the challenge "Magazine Cover".  What amazes me is how subjective the voting process can be, regardless of the photo quality. <b>I mean, twenty-five 1''s ???</b>. How more unfair can it be?  Anyway...<br/> <br/>Interesting facts though about the votes this photo received (total approx. 320 votes):<br/>Average Vote per <b>Commenters:8.807</b> (67 comments!)<br/>Average Vote per <b>Users w/ Cameras:</b> 6.577<br/>Average Vote per Users <b>w/out Cameras: 3.250</b> <br/> <br/> <br/> <br/>Now if you''ll excuse me, I''ve got to break the news to this model that a laughing horse beat her in the Magazine Cover challenge...<br/> <br/>Thanks.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-06-18 01:24:38.</i></td>', 'Thanks to everybody who left comments.  I appreciate the fact that most of you were very respectful in your comments even though the photo was riské for DPC. I knew when submiting this photo that it was risky.  But I honestly question its ranking position... I think it deserved more, especially in the context of the challenge "Magazine Cover".  What amazes me is how subjective the voting process can be, regardless of the photo quality. I mean, twenty-five 1''s ???. How more unfair can it be?  Anyway... Interesting facts though about the votes this photo received (total approx. 320 votes):Average Vote per Commenters:8.807 (67 comments!)Average Vote per Users w/ Cameras: 6.577Average Vote per Users w/out Cameras: 3.250    Now if you''ll excuse me, I''ve got to break the news to this model that a laughing horse beat her in the Magazine Cover challenge... Thanks.', '2003-06-18 01:04:46.000000', '2003-06-18 02:24:38.000000', 0),
