(328371, 24460, 2011, '<td valign="top">Great Photo and get win.  I knew it had to be you.  My sister got married at Auburn.   The lighting is awesome.  Again keep up the great work.</td>', 'Great Photo and get win.  I knew it had to be you.  My sister got married at Auburn.   The lighting is awesome.  Again keep up the great work.', '2003-06-18 01:23:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(328383, 24460, 1880, '<td valign="top">Way to go Sher, I gave this a 10 because it deserved it. One of my favorites of the challenge. Congrats on the ribbon.<br/> <br/>Bob</td>', 'Way to go Sher, I gave this a 10 because it deserved it. One of my favorites of the challenge. Congrats on the ribbon. Bob', '2003-06-18 01:26:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(328410, 24049, 2586, '<td valign="top">Thank you for the nice comments. The original image contains all the reflection and plenty of water above the heron''s head. I had to make a compromise, however, which was to crop somewhat in order to retain the most clarity on the face and notably the eye. That was worth sacrificing some space for. Ideally, i would have been a little closer to the heron. I stood on a rock at the edge of the water. Had i taken one step forward both the tripod and i would have fallen into the bay!<br/> <br/>I really love this guy and was delighted to encounter him very, very early on a Sunday morning. Actually, i feel a little proud of this image and that i was able to capture him . Several other pics i took of him will appear in my portfolio shortly.</td>', 'Thank you for the nice comments. The original image contains all the reflection and plenty of water above the heron''s head. I had to make a compromise, however, which was to crop somewhat in order to retain the most clarity on the face and notably the eye. That was worth sacrificing some space for. Ideally, i would have been a little closer to the heron. I stood on a rock at the edge of the water. Had i taken one step forward both the tripod and i would have fallen into the bay! I really love this guy and was delighted to encounter him very, very early on a Sunday morning. Actually, i feel a little proud of this image and that i was able to capture him . Several other pics i took of him will appear in my portfolio shortly.', '2003-06-18 01:35:56.000000', NULL, 0),
